atch (Exception)` swallows, while native-image raises `MissingReflectionRegistrationError`, which `extends Error` and sails right past that same catch block. That asymmetry is why the agent can \"see\" a reflective access attempt yet still produce metadata that's incomplete for native-image's stricter closed-world model — a recurring class of bug whenever Unsafe-based offset computation is on the hot path (common in Netty-derived libraries).\n- Comparing against `grpc-netty-shaded`'s metadata for the exact same `PlatformDependent0$6` condition was decisive here — rather than guessing at the right JSON shape, finding a sibling library that bundles the same Netty internals and already has the correct, working entry turned \"what should this look like\" into \"copy this.\"\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────","ttft_ms":3508,"type":"result","duration_ms":562382,"uuid":"90c2ef80-f55f-43a9-afcb-13769f1ed8d5","ttft_stream_ms":1924,"time_to_request_ms":142,"first_content_frame_ms":1924,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

